WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.500
[Introductory music] Web Accessibility Perspectives: Video Captions.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:12.000
Video isn't just about pictures, it's also about sound. Without the audio, you would have to guess what this film is about.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.500
[Silence — muted speaker on screen] Frustrating, isn't it? Not knowing what's going on. That's the situation for everyone who can't hear.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:25.000
[Click sound] Captions make videos accessible, which is also handy for people who want to watch video in loud environments.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:32.500
[Library chatter, librarian shushes: "Shhh!"] Or where you need to be very, very quiet.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:42.000
[Upbeat closing tone] Web accessibility: Essential for some, useful for all. Visit w3.org/WAI/perspectives for more information on Video Captions.
